      {
       "data": "Out[555]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline & \\text{(p1, p2, p3, scale)}\\\\\\hline\\text{reference vacuum} & \\left\\{1,\\frac{8}{5},-\\frac{3}{5},1\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 1: <Omega|(1 + r R)} & \\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1-3\\,r}{2\\,r+1} & \\frac{8}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5} & 2\\,r+1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 2: <Omega|(1 + r R\\^{}S)} & \\begin{pmatrix}1 & \\frac{16\\,r+8}{25\\,r+5} & \\frac{9\\,r-3}{25\\,r+5} & 5\\,r+1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{z} & \\left\\{2,-3,5\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "caf62e17-5797-4507-a1fb-311a2f95116f"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: $1-k_1R$ as one-site rotations (exact in $r=-k_1$, point above, $z=(2,-3,5)$)\n\nWith $d_a = 1-k_1z_a$:\n\n- **Site 1:** $\\langle\\Omega|(1-k_1R(\\theta_1)) = d_1\\;e_1^Te^{p_1\\frac{d_2}{d_1}E_{12}}e^{p_2E_{13}}e^{p_3E_{23}}\\otimes\\langle\\Omega_2|$ — exactly the $\\langle v_1|$ of $\\langle k_1^{u/h}Q_1\\rangle$ (`L2-mathcalA.tex`).\n- **Site 2:** $\\langle\\Omega|(1-k_1R^S(\\theta_2+2h)) = \\langle\\Omega_1|\\otimes d_3\\;e_1^Te^{p_1E_{12}}e^{p_2\\frac{d_1}{d_3}E_{13}}e^{p_3\\frac{d_2}{d_3}E_{23}}$.\n\nSite 1 rescales the $E_{12}$ angle (scale $d_1$); site 2 leaves $E_{12}$ and rescales the $E_{13},E_{23}$ angles, with $z_3$ in the role $z_1$ plays on site 1 (scale $d_3$). The site-2 image is **not** on the rotparams family ($p_3'/p_2' \\neq p_3/p_2$).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Eigenvalue of the localizing ratio in terms of Q's\n\nDiagonal frame, adjoint ⊗ adjoint, same point. For every eigenstate: $\\tau_a(u)$ as polynomials, weight $\\mu$, then the twisted Q's from the Baxter operators of `L2-mathcalA.wb` (cell 5): direct $Q_i=z_i^{u/h}q_i$, $\\deg q_i=2\\lambda_1-\\mu_i$; dual $Q^j=z_j^{-u/h}q^j$, $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$. Then test\n$$\\rho^S_A \\equiv \\mathrm{eig}_A\\,R^S(\\theta_2+2h) \\overset{?}{=} C\\,\\frac{q^3_A(\\theta_2+ah)}{q^3_A(\\theta_2+bh)}$$\nwith $C$ state-independent, scanning $a,b$; control: $\\rho_A=\\mathrm{eig}_A R(\\theta_1)$ against $q_1$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "prec = 60;\n(* joint eigenbasis of the commuting family (diagonal twist: generic simple spectrum) *)\nMmix = N[tGp[Gd][1][1/13] + 3 tGp[Gd][2][-2/9], prec];\n{evals, evecs} = Eigensystem[Mmix];\n(* tau_a(u) as polynomials: eigenvalue at deg+1 points, interpolated *)\nkk = First@Ordering[Abs[#], -1] & /@ evecs;\ntauEig[a_, x_] := Table[(N[tGp[Gd][a][x], prec] . evecs[[A]])[[kk[[A]]]]/evecs[[A, kk[[A]]]], {A, Length[evecs]}];\nupts = Range[0, 6]/7 + 1/11;\ntauPts = Table[tauEig[a, x], {a, 3}, {x, upts}];\ntauPoly = Table[Expand@InterpolatingPolynomial[Transpose[{upts, tauPts[[a, All, A]]}], u], {A, Length[evecs]}, {a, 3}];\nmuOf = Table[Round@Re[Table[(N[EE[i, i], prec] . evecs[[A]])[[kk[[A]]]]/evecs[[A, kk[[A]]]], {i, 3}]], {A, Length[evecs]}];\n(* check: tau polys reproduce the eigenvalue at a fresh point, and degrees *)\n{Max@Abs[Table[tauPoly[[A, 1]] /. u -> 5/3, {A, Length[evecs]}] - tauEig[1, 5/3]], Union[Exponent[Chop[#, 10^-40], u] & /@ Flatten[tauPoly]], Tally[muOf] // Length}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"677717\" data-output-id=\"53\" data-out-n=\"565\" data-sub-idx=\"12\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"39\" data-sub-start=\"12\" data-sub-end=\"12\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[565]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRcezAuXHRpbWVzIDEwXnstNTJ9LFxsZWZ0XHsyLDQsNlxyaWdodFx9LDE5XHJpZ2h0XH0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2141em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">{</span></span><span class=\"mord\">0.</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">52</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">19</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[565]= \\left\\{0.\\times 10^{-52},\\left\\{2,4,6\\right\\},19\\right\\}",
