      {
       "data": "Out[578]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{ratio} & \\text{a} & \\text{b} & \\text{rel. spread of C} & \\text{C}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 1: R(th1) vs q\\_1} & 2 & 1 & 0.\\times 10^{-51} & 2.\\,+0.\\times 10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{i}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 1: R(th1) vs q\\_1} & 3 & 1 & 0.984 & 1.00807571210+0.\\times 10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{i}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 1: R(th1) vs q\\_1} & 4 & 1 & 1.86 & 0.698982875285+0.\\times 10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{i}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 2: R\\^{}S(th2+2h) vs q\\^{}3} & 0 & 1 & 0.\\times 10^{-49} & 5.\\,+0.\\times 10^{-11}\\,\\mathrm{i}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 2: R\\^{}S(th2+2h) vs q\\^{}3} & 0 & -1 & 12.9 & -28.4808183332+0.\\times 10^{-11}\\,\\mathrm{i}\\\\\\hline\\text{site 2: R\\^{}S(th2+2h) vs q\\^{}3} & 0 & -2 & 15.9 & -103.527824845+0.\\times 10^{-10}\\,\\mathrm{i}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "26662fc4-ed19-4596-a23d-282c0d987679"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: ratio eigenvalues (all 64 states, relative spread of $C$ ~ $10^{-49}$ at 60 digits)\n\n$$\\mathrm{eig}_A\\,R(\\theta_1)=\\frac{Q_{1,A}(\\theta_1+2h)}{Q_{1,A}(\\theta_1+h)},\\qquad \\mathrm{eig}_A\\,R^S(\\theta_2+2h)=\\frac{Q^3_A(\\theta_2)}{Q^3_A(\\theta_2+h)},$$\nwith $Q_1=z_1^{u/h}q_1$, $Q^3=z_3^{-u/h}q^3$ (fitted constants $C=z_1=2$ and $C=z_3=5$ are exactly the twist factors). $R=t_{20}t_{10}^{-1}/\\nu_1(u+h)$ at $u=\\theta_1$, $R^S=t^S_{20}t^{S\\,-1}_{10}/\\nu_3(u-h)$ at $u=\\theta_2+2h$. So $\\langle\\Omega|(1-kR^S)|\\Psi_A\\rangle = \\big(1-k\\,Q^3_A(\\theta_2)/Q^3_A(\\theta_2+h)\\big)\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi_A\\rangle$, and $1-kR^S$ is the site-2 rotation above (scale $1-kz_3$).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Site-2 bracket vs $\\langle\\Omega|(1-kR^S)|\\Psi\\rangle$, directly from the eigenvectors\n\n$\\mathcal B_\\pm[k] = \\oint \\frac{Q^3(u)\\,k^{\\pm u/h}}{(u-\\theta_2)(u-\\theta_2-h)}$ (sum of the two residues), normalised by the residue at $\\theta_2$ or at $\\theta_2+h$; compared with $\\langle\\Omega|(1-kR^S(\\theta_2+2h))|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ for $\\Psi_A$ normalised to $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi_A\\rangle=1$. Independent of the ratio fit above: the right side uses the operator and the eigenvectors.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Om = N[kron[f1, f2], prec];\nkT = 3/7;\nopSide = Table[With[{psi = evecs[[A]]/(Om . evecs[[A]])}, Om . (psi - kT N[Rn2, prec] . psi)], {A, 64}];\nQ3[A_, x_] := N[zs[[3]], prec]^(-x/hh) qDual3[[A, 1]][x];\n(* residues of Q3(u) k^(s u/h)/((u - th2)(u - th2 - h)) at th2 and th2 + h *)\nres0[A_, s_] := Q3[A, th[2]] kT^(s th[2]/hh)/(-hh);\nres1[A_, s_] := Q3[A, th[2] + hh] kT^(s (th[2] + hh)/hh)/hh;\nbr[A_, s_, norm_] := (res0[A, s] + res1[A, s])/If[norm == 0, res0[A, s], res1[A, s]];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{If[s == 1, \"k^(+u/h)\", \"k^(-u/h)\"], If[nm == 0, \"Res at th2\", \"Res at th2+h\"], N[Max[Abs[Table[br[A, s, nm], {A, 64}] - opSide]], 3]}, {s, {1, -1}}, {nm, {0, 1}}] ~Flatten~ 1, {\"exponential\", \"normalised by\", \"max |bracket - <Omega|(1 - k R^S)|Psi>|\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
