style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-12.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-14.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.25em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.75em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[750]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{O1} & \\text{O2} & \\text{rank (pt 1)} & \\text{= a (x) b (pt 1)} & \\text{rank (pt 2)} & \\text{= a (x) b (pt 2)}\\\\\\hline\\text{R} & \\text{R\\^{}S} & 1 & \\mathrm{True} & 1 & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{R} & \\text{tS11} & 2 & \\mathrm{False} & 2 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{R} & \\text{R\\^{}S.tS11} & 2 & \\mathrm{False} & 2 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{t11} & \\text{R\\^{}S} & 2 & \\mathrm{False} & 2 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{t11} & \\text{tS11} & 3 & \\mathrm{False} & 3 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{t11} & \\text{R\\^{}S.tS11} & 3 & \\mathrm{False} & 3 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{R.t11} & \\text{R\\^{}S} & 2 & \\mathrm{False} & 2 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{R.t11} & \\text{tS11} & 3 & \\mathrm{False} & 3 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\text{R.t11} & \\text{R\\^{}S.tS11} & 4 & \\mathrm{False} & 4 & \\mathrm{False}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "9322df6f-6af8-442a-ac77-3b27610bd813"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Finding: the singlet-reaching products are NOT one-body (points 1 and 2, identical)\n\nOnly $R\\cdot R^S$ stays a product state, $=a\\otimes b$ (both are one-site rotations; singlet overlap 0). Every product involving $t_{11}$ or $t^S_{11}$ is entangled: rank 2–4, and $\\neq a\\otimes b$. So the singlet reach above comes entirely from covectors on the coupled space, which defeats the one-body reduction. Within genuinely one-body (product-state) constructions from these localized operators, the singlet is still not reached. — The earlier \"full reach\" table should be read with this caveat.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Exploration: the full one-body localized spaces in the two-site SoV span\n\nIdea: $\\langle\\Omega|\\mathcal A$ ($\\mathcal A$ = commutative transfer-matrix algebra) is everything, so every one-body covector $\\langle v|\\otimes\\langle\\Omega_2|$ is $\\langle\\Omega|O$ with $O\\in\\mathcal A$, and $\\langle v\\otimes\\Omega_2|\\Psi\\rangle$ is $O$'s eigenvalue. Look for *simple* such $O$ inside the 64-dim span of the two-site SoV recipe $O_{g_1}(\\theta_1)O_{g_2}(\\theta_2)$, $g\\in\\{100,110,111,200,210,211,220,221\\}$ (`L2-localizing-transfer.tex` found an 8-dim site-1-localized subspace, with site-2/site-1 mixed pairs). Here: reproduce it in these conventions, and look for the site-2 mirror (with the site-2 recipe at $\\theta_2+2h$ via $t^S$ and the site-1 one at $\\theta_1$).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "gLabels = {\"100\", \"110\", \"111\", \"200\", \"210\", \"211\", \"220\", \"221\"};\nOg[o_] := Module[{R = o[\"t20\"] . Inverse[o[\"t10\"]]}, <|\"100\" -> IdentityMatrix[d1 d2], \"110\" -> o[\"t10\"], \"111\" -> o[\"t11\"], \"200\" -> R, \"210\" -> o[\"t20\"], \"211\" -> R . o[\"t11\"], \"220\" -> R . o[\"t20\"], \"221\" -> R . o[\"t21\"]|>];\n(* covectors of all 64 two-site recipe states; site 1 at u1 with tower tw1, site 2 at u2 with tower tw2 *)\nrecipe2[tw1_, u1_, tw2_, u2_] := Module[{O1 = Og[towers[Gd, tw1, u1]], O2 = Og[towers[Gd, tw2, u2]]},\n   Association@Flatten@Table[{g1, g2} -> kron[f1, f2] . O1[g1] . O2[g2], {g1, gLabels}, {g2, gLabels}]];\n(* localized combinations: c.S in <any| (x) <Omega2| (site 1) or <Omega1| (x) <any| (site 2) *)\nlocSpan[st_, site_] := Module[{S = Values[st], V, ns},\n   V = If[site == 1, Table[kron[UnitVector[d1, k], f2], {k, d1}], Table[kron[f1, UnitVector[d2, k]], {k, d2}]];\n   ns = NullSpace[Transpose[Join[S, V]]];\n   {MatrixRank[S], Length[ns], RowReduce[ns[[All, 1 ;; Length[S]]]]}];\nsetPoint[pts4[[1]]];\nstA = recipe2[\"t\", th[1], \"t\", th[2]];\nstB = recipe2[\"t\", th[1], \"tS\", th[2] + 2 hh];\nlocAll = {{\"original basis (t at th1, t at th2)\", 1, locSpan[stA, 1]}, {\"original basis\", 2, locSpan[stA, 2]}, {\"mixed (t at th1, tS at th2+2h)\", 1, locSpan[stB, 1]}, {\"mixed\", 2, locSpan[stB, 2]}};\nGrid[Prepend[{#[[1]], #[[2]], #[[3, 1]], #[[3, 2]], Length[Union[Flatten[Position[#, _?(# != 0 &)] & /@ #[[3, 3]]]]]} & /@ locAll, {\"span\", \"localized on site\", \"rank of 64\", \"dim localized\", \"# labels involved\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
