  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: one-body localized states in the mixed SoV span (point 1, exact)\n\nMixed span: $\\langle\\Omega|O_{g_1}(\\theta_1)O_{g_2}(\\theta_2+2h)$, site 1 with `t`, site 2 with `tS`; rank 64. Minimal combinations localized on site 1 (site-2 factor $\\langle\\Omega_2|$), up to 3 labels — 7 of the 8 dimensions:\n\n| combination | one-body site-1 factor, in the single-site $L=1$ SoV basis $\\langle\\Omega_1|O^{(1)}_g(\\theta_1)$ | singlet |\n|---|---|---|\n| $100|100$, $111|100$, $200|100$, $211|100$ | exactly $100$, $111$, $200$, $211$ | 0 |\n| $\\{100|110,\\ 100|200,\\ 110|100\\}$ | span$\\{100,110,200\\}$ | 0 |\n| $\\{200|110,\\ 200|200,\\ 210|100\\}$ | span$\\{200,210\\}$ | 0 |\n| $\\{211|110,\\ 211|200,\\ 221|100\\}$ | span$\\{200,211,221\\}$ | **$\\neq0$** |\n\nSo, modulo the directly localized singles, the site-1 single-site states $110$, $210$, $221$ are also one-body reachable: **7 of the 8 single-site $L=1$ SoV states** ($220$ missing; needs $\\geq4$ labels). Site 2 is the exact mirror (`tS` at $\\theta_2+2h$ with site-1 `t` at $\\theta_1$ as the dressing), also reaching the singlet via $\\{100|221,\\ 110|211,\\ 200|211\\}$.\n\nMechanism: $t_{10}$ alone never localizes; it is *dressed* by the other site's $t^S_{10}$ and $R^S$ (resp. $t_{10}$, $R$). Q-form: singles are single Q-ratios ($R$: $Q_1$; $t_{11}(\\theta_1)$: $Q^2(\\theta_1+h)/Q^2(\\theta_1)$; $R^S$: $Q^3$; $t^S_{11}$: $Q^{23}$). The $t_{10}$ pieces are not single ratios; the triples do not fit a single-family linear bracket — open.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Finding the Q-form of $\\tau_1(u)$ (eigenvalue of $t_{\\{1,0\\}}$, unnormalised)\n\nAnsatz: $\\tau_1(x)=\\sum_{a=1}^3 c_a(x)\\,Q_a(x+\\alpha h)\\,Q^a(x+\\beta h)$, $c_a$ state-independent; all three $Q^a$ (dual Baxter) needed. Scan $\\alpha,\\beta$ at a generic $x$, then read off $c_a(x)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* c_a(x) of tau1(x) = sum_a c_a(x) Q_a(x+h) Q^a(x-h): sample, interpolate, factor *)\nxsC = Range[0, 10]/11 + 1/7;\ncSamples = Table[bilinFit[x, 1, -1][[4]], {x, xsC}];\ncPoly = Table[Expand@Chop[InterpolatingPolynomial[Transpose[{xsC, Re@cSamples[[All, a]]}], u], 10^-35], {a, 3}];\ncRes = Max@Table[Abs[bilinFit[x, 1, -1][[3]]], {x, {-3/5, 9/7}}];\ncCheck = Max@Table[Max@Abs[(cPoly /. u -> x) - bilinFit[x, 1, -1][[4]]], {x, {-3/5, 9/7}}];\n(* roots in units (u - th_s)/h *)\ncRoots = Table[Sort@Chop[N[Flatten[Table[(r - th[s])/hh, {s, 2}, {r, u /. NSolve[cPoly[[a]] == 0, u]}]], 8], 10^-15], {a, 3}];\n{\"degree\" -> Exponent[#, u] & /@ cPoly, \"leading coeff\" -> N[Coefficient[#, u, Exponent[#, u]] & /@ cPoly, 10], \"roots (u-th_s)/h\" -> cRoots, \"check at fresh x\" -> N[{cRes, cCheck}, 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
