  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: Q-form of the localized one-body functionals (point 1; coefficients at points 1 and 2)\n\n**Transfer-matrix eigenvalues (all 64 states, $\\sim10^{-49}$):**\n$$\\tau_1(x)=\\frac{K}{\\nu_2(x)}\\sum_a\\kappa_a\\,Q_a(x+h)\\,Q^a(x-h),\\qquad \\tau_2(x)=K'\\sum_a\\kappa'_a\\,Q^a(x+h)\\,Q_a(x-2h),$$\n$\\kappa:\\kappa'$ both $16:9:-25$ (monic normalisation), $K=-1/120$, $K'=-120$ at this point; $\\tau_3$ state-independent.\n\n**Localizing combinations** (ν-normalised, $T=\\theta_{12}/h$, confirmed at both points):\n- $X_1 = t^S_{10}(\\theta_2+2h)-\\tfrac12R^S(\\theta_2+2h)+(1-T)\\,t_{10}(\\theta_1)$: one-body on site 1, factor in span$\\{100,110,200\\}$. Mirror $X_2$ (swap sites/towers) same coefficients.\n- $Y_1 = R\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)\\big[t^S_{10}-\\tfrac12\\tfrac{(T-1)^2}{T(T-2)}R^S\\big](\\theta_2+2h)-\\tfrac12\\tfrac{T(T-1)}{T-2}\\,R\\,t_{21}(\\theta_1)$: one-body on site 1, factor in span$\\{200,211,221\\}$, **singlet overlap $\\neq0$**.\n\n**Eigenvalues in Q's** (verified against the operators, $X_1$: $\\sim10^{-50}$, $Y_1$: $\\sim10^{-30}$): substitute $R\\to Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)/Q_1(\\theta_1+h)$, $R^S\\to Q^3(\\theta_2)/Q^3(\\theta_2+h)$, $\\tau_1,\\tau_2$ bilinears above, $t_{21}=\\tau_2(\\theta_1)\\tau_1(\\theta_1+h)-\\tau_3$ ($\\tau_1(\\theta_1+h)$ at the $\\nu_2$ zero by the limit). So $\\langle v_{Y}\\otimes\\Omega_2|\\Psi\\rangle=\\mathrm{eig}(Y_1)\\,\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ is an explicit Q-expression for a one-body covector that reaches the singlet.\n\nOpen: a compact bracket form; $K,K'$, $\\kappa$ in closed form; the 8th state (220).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Classification: for which product states $\\langle v_1|\\otimes\\langle v_2|$ does the action localize?\n\nFor a site-1 operator $O$ and fixed site-2 covector $w$: $V_{\\rm loc}(O;w)=\\{v_1:(v_1\\otimes w)O=v_1'\\otimes w\\}$, a linear space. Mirror for site-2 operators with site 1 fixed. Also record whether $V_{\\rm loc}$ is **invariant** under $O$ (so the action can be iterated without leaving product states). Point 1, exact.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (a) bare extremal w: are the localized product states just left eigen-covectors of O? *)\neigenQ[O_, v_] := MatrixRank[{v, v . O}] == 1;\ntrivialCheck = Table[{k, Table[With[{B = vlocSite1[site1Ops[o], UnitVector[8, k]]}, AllTrue[B, eigenQ[site1Ops[o], kron[#, UnitVector[8, k]]] &]], {o, Keys[site1Ops]}]}, {k, {1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8}}];\n(* (b) rotated extremal w = e1.g: V_loc in the g-frame, i.e. V_loc . g^-1, by weight *)\ngR = PiSite[2, gRand[2]]; gR1 = PiSite[1, gRand[2]];\nwR = ext[2, True] . gR;\nframeContent[B_] := Module[{Bf = # . Inverse[gR1] & /@ B}, Union@Flatten[Table[If[Max[Abs[b[[k]]]] > 0, {wtsV[[k]]}, {}], {b, {Total[RandomInteger[{1, 9}, Length[Bf]] Bf]}}, {k, 8}], 2]];\nrotCheck = Table[{o, Length[vlocSite1[site1Ops[o], wR]], frameContent[vlocSite1[site1Ops[o], wR]]}, {o, {\"t11\", \"R\", \"R.t11\", \"t21\"}}];\n{trivialCheck, rotCheck}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"677717\" data-output-id=\"93\" data-out-n=\"888\" data-sub-idx=\"8\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"98\" data-sub-start=\"8\" data-sub-end=\"8\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[888]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-line-broken=\"1\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:16.2201em;vertical-align:-7.8601em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-r\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.3601em;\"><span style=\"top:-10.9701em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.46em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.86em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.46em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.8601em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"col-align-l\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.3601em;\"><span style=\"top:-10.9701em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.46em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.366em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.816em;\"></span><span class=\"