  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Summary: the SoV states localized on site 1, written as $t$'s on the vacuum\n\n**Setting.** Companion frame (twist $G_c$), adjoint $\\otimes$ adjoint. Vacuum $\\langle 0| = e_8^T\\otimes e_8^T$ (lowest weight on both sites, unrotated). All $t$'s are the companion-twisted fused transfer matrices of the two-site chain, unnormalised, and\n$$R(u) := t_{\\{2,0\\}}(u)\\,t_{\\{1,0\\}}(u)^{-1}.$$\nThe SoV basis is $\\langle x_{g_1|g_2}| = \\langle 0|\\,O_{g_1}(\\theta_1)\\,O_{g_2}(\\theta_2)$ with\n$O_{100}=1,\\ O_{110}=t_{10},\\ O_{111}=t_{11},\\ O_{200}=R,\\ O_{210}=t_{20},\\ O_{211}=R\\,t_{11},\\ O_{220}=R\\,t_{20},\\ O_{221}=R\\,t_{21}$.\nChecked: these 64 states are exactly the left eigenvectors of $B(u)=T_{11}QM_{12,12}(u+h)+T_{21}QM_{12,13}(u+h)$ (untwisted $T$), and their wave functions are the Ryan–Volin products (arXiv:2002.12341, eq. 5.22).\n\n**\"Localized on site 1\"** means the covector equals $\\langle v|\\otimes e_8^T$: site 2 stays exactly in its vacuum. The space of these is 8-dimensional and is spanned by ($T=\\theta_{12}/h$):\n\n| # | localized covector | SoV labels | singlet |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | $\\langle 0\\|$ | $100\\|100$ | 0 |\n| 2 | $\\langle 0\\|\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)$ | $111\\|100$ | 0 |\n| 3 | $\\langle 0\\|\\,R(\\theta_1)$ | $200\\|100$ | 0 |\n| 4 | $\\langle 0\\|\\,R(\\theta_1)\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)$ | $211\\|100$ | 0 |\n| 5 | $\\langle 0\\|\\,\\big[\\,t_{10}(\\theta_1)-\\tfrac{1}{T}\\,R(\\theta_2)\\,\\big]$ | $110\\|100,\\ 100\\|200$ | 0 |\n| 6 | $\\langle 0\\|\\,\\big[\\,t_{20}(\\theta_1)-\\tfrac{2}{T+1}\\,R(\\theta_1)R(\\theta_2)\\,\\big]$ | $210\\|100,\\ 200\\|200$ | 0 |\n| 7 | $\\langle 0\\|\\,\\big[\\,R(\\theta_1)t_{20}(\\theta_1)-\\tfrac{2(T-1)}{(T+1)(T-2)}\\,t_{20}(\\theta_1)R(\\theta_2)\\,\\big]$ | $220\\|100,\\ 210\\|200$ | 0 |\n| **8** | $\\boxed{\\ \\langle 0\\|\\,R(\\theta_1)\\,\\Big[\\,t_{21}(\\theta_1)-\\dfrac{1}{T+1}\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)\\,R(\\theta_2)\\,\\Big]\\ }$ | $221\\|100,\\ 211\\|200$ | **$\\neq 0$** |\n\nRows 1–4 are single SoV states (site 2 in its vacuum label 100). Rows 5–8 are pairs: a site-1 excitation $g_1^+|100$ plus the state $g_1|200$ in which site 2 is excited by $R(\\theta_2)$. Neither member of a pair is localized alone (e.g. $\\langle0|R(\\theta_1)t_{21}(\\theta_1)$ is entangled); the $R(\\theta_2)$ term with exactly this coefficient removes the site-2 excitation. All coefficients checked at two points (different $h$, $\\theta$, $z$); they depend only on $T$.\n\n**The singlet.** Row 8 is the only one of the eight with a singlet component. As a functional of a Bethe state (normalised by $\\langle0|\\Psi\\rangle=1$) its value is the eigenvalue\n$$\\rho(\\theta_1)\\Big[\\tau_{21}(\\theta_1)-\\frac{1}{T+1}\\,\\tau_{11}(\\theta_1)\\,\\rho(\\theta_2)\\Big],$$\nwith $\\rho,\\tau_{11},\\tau_{21}$ the eigenvalues of $R,t_{11},t_{21}$. In Ryan–Volin form (monic $Q$'s, their normalisation) it is $\\propto Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)\\big[D_1(0,2)+\\frac{h}{\\theta_{12}-h}D_1(0,1)\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_2+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_2+h)}\\big]$, $D_1(a,b)=Q_1(\\theta_1+ah)Q_2(\\theta_1+bh)-Q_2(\\theta_1+ah)Q_1(\\theta_1+bh)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# The singlet functional from Q's\n\nOperator side (eigenvalues from the transfer-matrix polynomials, frame-independent): $E^{\\rm op}_A=\\rho(\\theta_1)\\big[\\tau_{21}(\\theta_1)-\\tfrac{1}{T+1}\\tau_{11}(\\theta_1)\\rho(\\theta_2)\\big]$, $\\rho(u)=\\frac{\\tau_1(u)\\tau_1(u+h)-\\tau_2(u+h)}{\\tau_1(u)}$, $\\tau_{11}=\\tau_2$, $\\tau_{21}(u)=\\tau_2(u)\\tau_1(u+h)-\\tau_3(u+h)$.\n\nQ side (Ryan–Volin, localization coefficient $1/(T-1)$, no fit): $E^Q_A=\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_1+h)}\\cdot\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_2+h)D(0,2)+\\frac1{T-1}Q_1(\\theta_2+2h)D(0,1)}{Q_1(\\theta_2+h)D(-1,0)}$, $D(a,b)=Q_1(\\theta_1+ah)Q_2(\\theta_1+bh)-Q_2(\\theta_1+ah)Q_1(\\theta_1+bh)$. Test $E^{\\rm op}/E^Q$ = one constant over all 64 states, at both points.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: the singlet-reaching one-body functional in Q's (points 1 and 2, all 64 states, $\\sim10^{-48}$)\n\nWith $\\langle 0|\\Psi\\rangle=1$,\n$$\\langle 0|\\,R(\\theta_1)\\Big[t_{21}(\\theta_1)-\\tfrac{1}{T+1}\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)R(\\theta_2)\\Big]|\\Psi\\rangle\\;=\\;C\\;\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_1+h)}\\;\\frac{D(0,2)+\\dfrac{1}{T-1}\\,D(0,1)\\,\\dfrac{Q_1(\\theta_2+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_2+h)}}{D(-1,0)},$$\n$D(a,b)=Q_1(\\theta_1+ah)Q_2(\\theta_1+bh)-Q_2(\\theta_1+ah)Q_1(\\theta_1+bh)$, $T=\\theta_{12}/h$, $C$ state-independent (absorbs the $z_a^{\\theta/h}$ of the monic normalisation). Equivalently, as a $2\\times2$ determinant with one \"dressed\" column:\n$$\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_1+h)\\,D(-1,0)}\\;\\det\\begin{pmatrix}Q_1(\\theta_1) & Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)+\\frac{\\rho_2}{T-1}Q_1(\\theta_1+h)\\\\ Q_2(\\theta_1) & Q_2(\\theta_1+2h)+\\frac{\\rho_2}{T-1}Q_2(\\theta_1+h)\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\rho_2=\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_2+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_2+h)}.$$\nThe only site-2 input is $\\rho_2$ — the eigenvalue of $R(\\theta_2)$ — which enters exactly where the operator has its site-2 dressing term.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Towards a contour-integral form of the singlet functional\n\n$F\\propto Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)\\big[D_1(0,2)Q_1(\\theta_2+h)+c\\,D_1(0,1)Q_1(\\theta_2+2h)\\big]$, $c=\\frac1{T-1}$. The bracket is a double contour: $u$ around $\\theta_1+h,\\theta_1+2h$ (the second $D_1$ argument), $v$ around $\\theta_2+h,\\theta_2+2h$, integrand $D_1(0,u)Q_1(v)\\,\\mu(u,v)$, with $\\mu$ killing the diagonal pairs and weighting the anti-diagonal pairs $c:1$. Search (symbolic in $T$, $h=1$): $\\mu=\\frac{N(u,v)\\,f_1(u)f_2(v)}{(u-\\theta_1-h)(u-\\theta_1-2h)(v-\\theta_2-h)(v-\\theta_2-2h)}$, $N\\in\\{(u-v-\\theta_{12}),(u-v-\\theta_{12})^2\\}$, $f_1=\\prod(u-\\theta_2-a)^{\\pm1}$, $f_2=\\prod(v-\\theta_1-b)^{\\pm1}$ (up to two factors each), also a cross factor $(u-v-s)^{\\pm1}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Finding: no factorized double-contour form\n\nNo measure of the searched form reproduces $c=\\frac1{T-1}$ (573 insertions × 2 numerators; base ratio with no insertion is $\\mp1$). Structural reason: at the poles $u=\\theta_1+ph$, $v=\\theta_2+qh$ every such insertion is degree 0 in $T$ ($u-v-\\theta_{12}=p-q$; $(u-\\theta_2-a)$, $(v-\\theta_1-b)$ give $(T+\\alpha)/(T+\\beta)$), while $c\\to0$ as $T\\to\\infty$ (sites decouple). The $1/\\theta_{12}$ fall-off is what residues of a **single-variable bracket with poles on both sites** produce (cross-site pole differences $\\theta_{12}\\pm nh$), as in the two-site brackets of `L2-det-mathcalA`. That is the next ansatz.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Replacing $t^{(1)}_{11}(\\theta_1)$ by an arbitrary combination of quantum minors\n\nSite-1 family after undoing $g_0$: $\\langle v_1|g_0^{-1}=(1-k_1z_1)\\,e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}$. Conjugation by $g_0$ maps the span of all quantum minors to itself, so the question is: can $w=e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}\\,M$, $M\\in\\mathrm{span}$ of single-site quantum minors at $\\theta_1$, give $\\langle w\\otimes e_1^T|\\text{singlet}\\rangle\\neq0$? Weight count: the singlet needs two units in slot 3; each $2\\times2$ minor has distinct rows, hence at most one $E_{j3}$. Check numerically, and compare with products of two minors.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* natural quadratic one-body operators on site 1 (single-site twisted t's), evaluated at th1 + n h *)\nt1s[x_] := tGsite[1][1][x]; t2s[x_] := tGsite[1][2][x]; t3s[x_] := tGsite[1][3][x];\nt22s[x_] := t2s[x] . t2s[x + hh] - t3s[x + hh] . t1s[x];\nquadOps = Join[\n   Table[\"t22(th1+\" <> ToString[n] <> \"h)\" -> t22s[th[1] + n hh], {n, -2, 2}],\n   Flatten@Table[\"t11(th1+\" <> ToString[m] <> \"h) t11(th1+\" <> ToString[n] <> \"h)\" -> t2s[th[1] + m hh] . t2s[th[1] + n hh], {m, -1, 1}, {n, m, 2}]];\nGrid[Prepend[{#[[1]], N[singEff[w0 . #[[2]]], 5]} & /@ quadOps, {\"one-body operator on site 1\", \"singlet overlap of (w0 M) (x) e1\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"677717\" data-output-id=\"121\" data-out-n=\"1055\" data-sub-idx=\"4\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"140\" data-sub-start=\"6\" data-sub-end=\"6\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[1055]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:18.04em;vertical-align:-8.75em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.29em;\"><span style=\"top:-11.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:18em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-8.75em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-11.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">one-body operator on site 1</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">t22(th1+-2h)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">t22(th1+-1h)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" s