   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: $[3,1,0]\\otimes[3,1,0]$\n\nThe scan is exact and identical at points 1 and 2, with 14 localizing $(a,b,r,s)$ as for the adjoint. Vacuum $e_{15}=(0,1,3)$. Site-1 results: $e_{14}=(0,2,2)$ (vacuum $+\\alpha_{23}$), $e_{11}=(1,1,2)$ ($+\\alpha_{13}$, the $gl_2$ singlet in pattern row $\\{1,1\\}$), $e_9=(1,2,1)$ ($+\\alpha_{13}+\\alpha_{23}$), $e_{13}=(0,3,1)$ ($+2\\alpha_{23}$).\n\n| $(a,b,r,s)$ | where | adjoint | $[3,1,0]$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $(1,2,0,1)$ | $v=\\theta_1$ | $e_5$ | $e_{11}$ |\n| $(1,2,0,1)$ | $u=v=\\theta_1+2h$ | $0$ | **$e_{13}$ (new)** |\n| $(2,2,0,2)$ | $u=\\theta_1$ | $e_5$ | $e_{11}$ |\n| $(2,2,1,2)$ | $u=\\theta_1+2h$ | $e_7$ | $e_{14}$ |\n| $(2,2,0,1)$ | $(\\theta_1+2h,\\theta_1)$ | $e_3$ | $e_9$ |\n| $(1,2,1,2)$ | all | vacuum | vacuum |\n\nSo every adjoint solution carries over, with the same special points and the same weight shift from the vacuum. The one addition, $P_{1,0}(\\theta_1{+}2h)P_{2,1}(\\theta_1{+}2h)-P_{2,0}(\\theta_1{+}2h)P_{1,1}(\\theta_1{+}2h)$, shifts by $2\\alpha_{23}$. That weight does not exist in the adjoint, where $\\langle0|X=0$ exactly at that point (checked at point 2). Note: the kernel's `pb*` definitions are left at adjoint, point 2.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* [3,2,0]^2 scan at both points, then per-solution site-1 support and GT weights *)\npb320s1 = Quiet[pbRescanRep[{3, 2, 0}, 1/3, {2/7, -5/11}], Solve::svars];\npb320s2 = Quiet[pbRescanRep[{3, 2, 0}, 1/2, {3/13, -4/17}], Solve::svars];\npbSupN[it_, n1_] := {it[[1]], Table[{sol /. {uu -> \"u\", vv -> \"v\"}, Flatten[Position[Expand[(pbW @@ it[[1]]) /. pbLabVal[sol]][[All, n1]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]}, {sol, it[[2]]}]};\npb320sup = pbSupN[#, dim[{3, 2, 0}]] & /@ pb320s2;\n{dim[{3, 2, 0}], Length[pb320s1], pb320s1[[All, 1 ;; 2]] === pb320s2[[All, 1 ;; 2]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"400495\" data-output-id=\"15\" data-out-n=\"141\" data-sub-idx=\"5\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"157\" data-sub-start=\"5\" data-sub-end=\"5\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[141]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRcezE1LDE0LFxtYXRocm17VHJ1ZX1ccmlnaHRcfQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">14</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[141]= \\left\\{15,14,\\mathrm{True}\\right\\}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "3a57a38e-2abe-40e9-adbb-729ebc445eef"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: $[3,2,0]\\otimes[3,2,0]$\n\nThe scan is exact and identical at points 1 and 2. It has the same 14 localizing $(a,b,r,s)$ as the adjoint, and no extra isolated point. Vacuum $e_{15}=(0,2,3)$.\n\n| $(a,b,r,s)$ | where | site-1 result |\n|---|---|---|\n| $(1,2,0,1)$, $(2,2,0,2)$ | $\\theta_1$ | $e_{12}=(1,2,2)$, $+\\alpha_{13}$ |\n| $(2,2,1,2)$ | $u=\\theta_1+3h$ | $e_{14}=(0,3,2)$, $+\\alpha_{23}$ |\n| $(2,2,0,1)$ | $(\\theta_1+3h,\\theta_1)$ | $e_{10}=(1,3,1)$, $+\\alpha_{13}+\\alpha_{23}$ |\n\nThe second special point moves: $\\theta_1+2h$ for $[2,1,0]$ and $[3,1,0]$, but $\\theta_1+3h$ here, consistent with $\\theta_1+(\\lambda_2+1)h$. The $[3,1,0]$-only $+2\\alpha_{23}$ solution does not appear: from $(0,2,3)$ that would need weight $(0,4,1)$, which is not in $[3,2,0]$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Localized P-bilinears: to the diagonal frame, undo $g_0$, which highest-weight states are reached? (adjoint)\n\nSame recipe as cells 30–32, 64, 73. The diagonal-frame covector is $\\langle v_c|\\,\\Pi(P)\\otimes\\Pi(P)$. The site-2 factor $e_8^T\\Pi(P)$ is the rotparams vacuum $e_1^Tg_0$, and $g_0$ is undone globally ($g_0^{-1}\\otimes g_0^{-1}$) so that site 2 sits at $e_1^T$. Then overlap with the highest-weight states of $V\\otimes V$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* self-contained: adjoint x adjoint at a point {h, th1, th2, z}; pb* machinery from cell 155 *)\npbPi[g_] := Module[{l21, l31, l32, dd1, dd2, dd3, u12, u13, u23, L, D, U, s, lg, ug, wts},\n   L = {{1, 0, 0}, {l21, 1, 0}, {l31, l32, 1}}; U = {{1, u12, u13}, {0, 1, u23}, {0, 0, 1}}; D = DiagonalMatrix[{dd1, dd2, dd3}];\n   s = First@Solve[Thread[Flatten[L . D . U - g] == 0], {l21, l31, l32, dd1, dd2, dd3, u12, u13, u23}]; {L, D, U} = {L, D, U} /. s;\n   lg = (L - IdentityMatrix[3]) - (L - IdentityMatrix[3]) . (L - IdentityMatrix[3])/2; ug = (U - IdentityMatrix[3]) - (U - IdentityMatrix[3]) . (U - IdentityMatrix[3])/2;\n   wts = Transpose[Table[Diagonal[Normal[pbE[i, i]]], {i, 3}]];\n   MatrixExp[Normal[Sum[lg[[i, j]] pbE[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]]] . DiagonalMatrix[Times @@ (Diagonal[D]^#) & /@ wts] . MatrixExp[Normal[Sum[ug[[i, j]] pbE[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]]]];\npbBack[{h_, t1_, t2_, z_}] := Module[{Pv, PiP, f2, sol, g0, g0i, EEg, hws, wt, groups, locs, res, td, chi},\n   Quiet[pbRescanRep[{2, 1, 0}, h, {t1, t2}]];\n   Pv = Transpose[{#^2, #, 1} & /@ z]; PiP = pbPi[Pv];\n   chi = {Total[z], -(z[[1]] z[[2]] + z[[1]] z[[3]] + z[[2]] z[[3]]), Times @@ z};\n   (* intertwiner check t_c = Pi(P) t_d Pi(P)^-1 at one u *)\n   td = Sum[z[[i]] pbT[i, i][3/7], {i, 3}];\n   (* site-2 factor e8.Pi(P) = c e1.g0, g0 = e^{p1 E12} e^{p2 E13} e^{p3 E23} *)\n   f2 = UnitVector[8, 8] . PiP;\n   g0[p1_, p2_, p3_] := MatrixExp[p1 Normal[pbE[1, 2]]] . MatrixExp[p2 Normal[pbE[1, 3]]] . MatrixExp[p3 Normal[pbE[2, 3]]];\n   sol = First@Solve[Thread[UnitVector[8, 1] . g0[p1, p2, p3] == cc f2], {p1, p2, p3, cc}];\n   g0i = Inverse[g0[p1, p2, p3] /. sol];\n   EEg[i_, j_] := KroneckerProduct[Normal[pbE[i, j]], IdentityMatrix[8]] + KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[8], Normal[pbE[i, j]]];\n   hws = NullSpace[Join[EEg[1, 2], EEg[2, 3]]];\n   wt[v_] := Module[{j = First@FirstPosition[v, _?(# != 0 &)]}, Table[(EEg[i, i] . v)[[j]]/v[[j]], {i, 3}]];\n   groups = GatherBy[hws, wt];\n   (* the four nontrivial localized bilinears, u free set to 1/5 where it is free *)\n   locs = {\"(1,2,0,1) v=th1\" -> {{1, 2, 0, 1}, {uu -> 1/5, vv -> t1}}, \"(2,2,0,2) u=th1\" -> {{2, 2, 0, 2}, {uu -> t1, vv -> 1/5}},\n     \"(2,2,1,2) u=th1+2h\" -> {{2, 2, 1, 2}, {uu -> t1 + 2 h, vv -> 1/5}}, \"(2,2,0,1) (th1+2h,th1)\" -> {{2, 2, 0, 1}, {uu -> t1 + 2 h, vv -> t1}},\n     \"reference: e1 (x) e8 (companion)\" -> None};\n   res = Table[Module[{vc, vd, w, m},\n      vc = If[l[[2]] === None, Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[8, 1], UnitVector[8, 8]]], Flatten[(pbW @@ l[[2, 1]]) /. l[[2, 2]]]];\n      vd = vc . KroneckerProduct[PiP, PiP]; w = vd . KroneckerProduct[g0i, g0i]; m = ArrayReshape[w, {8, 8}];\n      {l[[1]], MatrixRank[ArrayReshape[vc, {8, 8}]], MatrixRank[m], MatrixRank[{First@Select[m, Norm[#] > 0 &], UnitVector[8, 1]}] == 1,\n       Table[MatrixRank[Table[{w . hv}, {hv, g}]], {g, groups}], w . First[Select[hws, wt[#] == {2, 2, 2} &]]}], {l, locs}];\n   {pbt[1, chi][3/7] == PiP~KroneckerProduct~PiP . td . Inverse[PiP~KroneckerProduct~PiP], wt[First[#]] -> Length[#] & /@ groups, res}];\npbBackRes = pbBack /@ {{1/3, 2/7, -5/11, {2, -3, 5}}, {1/2, 3/13, -4/17, {3, -7/2, 11/4}}};\nGrid[Join[{{\"point\", \"localized state\", \"rank (companion)\", \"rank after Pi(P), g0^-1\", \"site 2 = e1?\", \"reached hw sectors \" <> ToString[pbBackRes[[1, 2]]], \"singlet overlap\"}},\n   Flatten[Table[Prepend[r, i], {i, 2}, {r, pbBackRes[[i, 3]]}], 1]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
